        "thinking": "Good - `dnsLookup` is used in `defaultInviteResolutionLookup`, which is only called when resolving invite URLs (part of the DNS test route). It's not in the main members/invites CRUD paths.\n\nSimilarly, `path.resolve` and `resolvePaperclipSkillsDir` are used for reading local SKILL.md files, not for the main members/invites endpoints.\n\nSo the main members/invites/join-request routes in `accessRoutes` are pure DB operations and will work correctly via the bridge. The DNS-dependent route (invite resolution test) will fail at runtime with the DNS shim error, but that's acceptable.\n \nI'm reconsidering whether to include `companySkillRoutes` at all. Most routes there depend on `ensureSkillInventoryCurrent`, which uses `fs.stat` and would fail with 500 errors. Since `cf-extra-routes.ts` already provides the working list endpoint, adding these routes would just introduce non-functional ones. But I'm already including them in my edit, so I need to decide whether to keep them despite the failures or remove them entirely.\n\nActually, 501 is better than 500 for unsupported operations in Cloudflare, so I should remove `companySkillRoutes` from the bridge. Though I should verify which routes actually depend on filesystem operations first, since some might work fine.",
